[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-7352e01c-65e8-4706-ad99-cd3de7763653\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research papers</p></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"7352e01c-65e8-4706-ad99-cd3de7763653\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>SAGE: Signal-Amplified Guided Embeddings for Vulnerability Detection</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><p>While Large Language Models (LLMs) have achieved milestones in automated software engineering, their application to vulnerability detection remains constrained by a notable sensitivity barrier. Despite advancements in graph-based analysis and supervised fine-tuning, existing paradigms frequently struggle to isolate the fine-grained, sparse semantic deviations characteristic of vulnerabilities from the dominant background of functional logic. We argue that this limitation stems from a notable architectural phenomenon we term \\textbf{Signal Submersion}. Our analysis reveals that while vulnerability-relevant features are activated in intermediate layers, these sparse signals occupy a disproportionately small magnitude and are substantially diminished by global semantic representations.</p>\n<p>To address this, we propose \\textbf{SAGE} (\\textbf{S}ignal-\\textbf{A}mplified \\textbf{G}uided \\textbf{E}mbeddings), a framework that transitions from passive inference to active signal amplification. SAGE employs a task-conditional Sparse Autoencoder (SAE) to project entangled representations onto a high-dimensional sparse manifold, mechanistically decoupling and resurfacing faint vulnerability signals. Extensive evaluations on BigVul, PrimeVul, and the zero-day benchmark PreciseBugs demonstrate that SAGE establishes new state-of-the-art performance. Notably, SAGE achieves relative MCC gains of up to 318% on unseen distributions and enables a 7B model to outperform 34B generalist baselines, validating that mechanistic disentanglement is a more efficient path to security than simply increasing model size.</p>\n<p></p><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/zhengyangshan\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Zhengyang Shan<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Shandong University</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/qianxu\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">QianXu <span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Shandong University</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/jiayunxin\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Jiayun Xin<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Shandong University</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/minghuixu\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Minghui Xu<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Shandong University</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/yuezhang6\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Yue Zhang<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Shandong University</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/zhenyang\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Zhen Yang\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/zhenyang/87932c38-4740-43b4-9515-a9c8128e3dc8/micro-avatar?1792875585000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Zhen Yang<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Shandong University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/haowu4\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Hao Wu\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/haowu4/c2926523-cb0d-4ae5-a0f6-6e58a3d7e799/micro-avatar?1792875588000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Hao Wu<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Nanjing University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/xiuzhencheng\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Xiuzhen Cheng<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Shandong University</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers/50/SAGE-Signal-Amplified-Guided-Embeddings-for-Vulnerability-Detection\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"btn btn-default navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-new-window\"></span> All Details</a></span><a href=\"#\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"btn btn-default\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span> Close</a></div></div></div></div>"},{ "action": "runscript", "value": "$('#modal-7352e01c-65e8-4706-ad99-cd3de7763653').modal({ backdrop: 'static', keyboard: true}, 'show');" },
